    T83
        title       Fast test commands again: suite, stress and faults with no regression from the baseline
        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T84]
        description
            Make the test commands fast again: the package suite, `nub run test:stress` and `nub run faults` with no
            regression from the measured baseline without a named cause, and no gate weakened.

            **Why now:** the 06:00 wake on 2026-11-17 timed HEAD 9d45d087 in a clean worktree: suite 33 s, stress 115 s,
            faults 172 s, against the 313e8a45 baseline of 12 s, 9 s and 28 s. T82's grown fixtures (S3 x 64, L1 x 64,
            1,024-send Stories) and T9's triple-reload check added the load, and T9 raised the stress sweeps' timeout to
            230 s to fit them under the faults run.

            **Read first:** @task.V3.T75 (the last speed pass and its comments), code:tools/faults/run.ts,
            `packages/flow-state-v3/tests/rules/`, `packages/flow-state-v3/tests/generated/`, the Epic's `instructions`
            (Speed; Big test commands run at the end of a Task).

            **Risk:** speed must not weaken a gate: every fault is caught by the same tests, the dead core still gets a
            full run, every scenario T82 and T9 built still runs in the default suite or behind the stress flag, and no
            Story's count shrinks except by a re-measurement recorded in the Story (@plan.Pending.D23). If a budget
            can't be met without cutting coverage, the lead reports the trade-off instead of cutting.

            **Approach:** measure first (time per file, per sweep, per fault), then fix the slowest causes; set a new
            speed baseline in V3.log at the close.

            May change: `packages/flow-state-v3/tests/`, `packages/flow-state-v3/fixtures/` (sample selection only),
            `tools/faults/`, `tools/stress/`, `vite.config.ts`, `package.json` scripts. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a faster run that drops a scenario or a fault → caught by the same Story ids, test counts and
            caught list, before and after.
        acceptance
            - Timings before and after, alone on this machine, are in a Task comment: the package suite, `nub run
              test:stress` and `nub run faults`, each per file or per fault for the slowest ten.
            - The baseline is re-measured and recorded at the Task's start; no regression from it without a named cause;
              before and after numbers are reported, and where a regression stays, the comment names what each lost
              second buys and the lead asks the user.
            - Each fixture Story's count is set from the bench and recorded in the Story (fixtures.md).
            - The same Story ids, test counts and fault caught list hold before and after; the dead core still runs the
              full suite.
            - No timeout is raised without a measured reason.
            - Every test-tooling guard has one source and a measured size (the user, 2026-11-17, Q5 A): the Story turn,
              settle-task and advance limits; the faults run's timeout, copies (from CPU and memory) and output buffer;
              the 230 s and 60 s test timeouts; the generator's weights, lengths and shrink budgets; the bench's warm-up
              from a stability check that reports variance; Story advances read the capture interval instead of writing
              5 s.
            - `nub run check` and `nub run lint:rules` pass; a new speed note with the baseline is in V3.log.
