    T85
        title       The step indexes the World and drafts its maps: no whole-world scans or whole-map copies
        status      open
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T9]
        description
            The step stops scanning the whole World and copying whole maps: actor keys are carried on identities, the
            World keeps per-step indexes, and a step edits one draft of its maps instead of copying a map per change.

            **Why now:** the performance audit
            (code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/performance-architecture-2026-11-17.md, findings 6, 7, 10 and 11)
            measured `actorKey` strings built per call at 13 % self time of `session/long`, `withEntry` whole-map copies
            at 5.7 % self (O(N^2) with an unbounded mailbox once D24 lands), and whole-world scans per step. The turn
            itself is 1 to 2 % of a run.

            **Read first:** the audit's findings 6, 7, 10 and 11 with their evidence; @spec.Turn, @spec.Actors;
            @plan.Pending.D24; code:wiki/conventions/fixtures.md.

            **Risk:** a draft that leaks between steps or an index that drifts from the World would lose or double an
            ending; every existing Story and run rule must hold unchanged, and the core stays pure and synchronous.

            May change: `packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/`, `tests/`, `bench/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a faster step that skips a rule's check → caught by the same Story ids, run rules and fault
            caught list before and after.
        acceptance
            - Profiles of `transfers/long`, `session/long` and a stress Story before and after, alone on this machine,
              in a Task comment, with each finding's share before and after.
            - Actor keys are built once per identity, World lookups use per-World indexes, and a step's map edits go
              through one draft; no whole-map copy per change remains on the step path.
            - A Story with many actors and a deep mailbox shows step cost grows with the work done, not with World size,
              timed on the bench.
            - The same Story ids, test counts and fault caught list hold before and after; `nub run check` passes.
